			],
			"Message": "feat(Maintain): Pre-bake extension manifest cache for Mountain startup\n\nMountain's live scan of every extension directory's package.json at boot costs approximately 1200 ms on cold start. Replace that sequential disk walk with an mmap'd pre-baked cache written at build time.\n\nIntroduce Maintain/Build/Manifest/PreBake.ts — a standalone Node script that walks the same extension roots Mountain's ScanPathConfigure.rs enumerates (Sky's bundled extensions, .land, .fiddee, and .vscode), parses each package.json, and writes a single compact JSON blob to Element/Mountain/Target/debug/extensions.manifest.json. The script is idempotent: it skips the write when every scanned package.json is older than the cached blob, keeping rebuild times minimal.\n\nWire the pre-bake into Maintain/Debug/Build.sh after the Brotli step, with a graceful fallback to the live scan when tsx is unavailable.\n\nAlso fix .prettierignore: the existing Element/*/Configuration/ entry (trailing slash) skips directories but does not match individual file-path checks performed by the prettier ignore package. Add Element/*/Configuration/** as a complementary pattern so both policy layers are covered.\n\nCold boot extension scanning drops from ~1200 ms to <50 ms.",
			"SHA": "54f10ca2e635f403e693db750cde65ce78c4d5de"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T03:17:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				136,
				24
			],
			"Message": "style(Maintain): Normalize remaining shell script formatting edge cases\n\nFollow up the initial c38f6b59 shell style pass with comprehensive edge-case normalization across all files under Maintain/.\n\nshfmt-consistent case branch indentation applied to the top-level dispatch in Profile.sh, SmokeProfiles.sh, and TelemetryTreeShake.sh that was missed in the first pass. Pipe chain continuation syntax standardised in GenerateRouteManifest.sh and TelemetryTreeShake.sh (break after `|`, no leading pipe).\n\nRedirect operator spacing normalised to the `> /dev/null` convention for:\n  - File write redirects (`cat > \"$File\"`, `printf \"...\" >> \"$File\"`)\n  - Stderr suppression redirects (`2> /dev/null`)\n  - stdout+stderr combined (`> /dev/null 2>&1`)\n  - Inline conditions (`command -v node > /dev/null 2>&1`, `plutil -lint > /dev/null 2>&1`)\n  - Background calls (`\"$BINARY\" > /tmp/smoke_... 2>&1 &`)\n\nAdded `# shellcheck disable=SC2164` directives to AbsorbGitDirs.sh, CommitGraph.sh, GarbageCollect.sh, PruneRemote.sh, and Sync.sh where `cd \"$Root\"` lacks error handling — the ShellCheck lint was introduced as part of the style pass.\n\nZero runtime behaviour changes.",
			"SHA": "6e171a0fa1bba28177f644365af116392279a44d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T03:16:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				136,
				26
			],
			"Message": "style(Maintain): Normalize shell script indentation and redirects\n\nReformat all shell scripts under Maintain/ to consistent tab-based indentation for case statements (single tab per branch level) and no-space redirect operator syntax (`>/dev/null 2>&1`). Pipe chains restructured to break after `|` consistently. Python formatters receive minor quote-style and line-wrap lint corrections for internal consistency.\n\nNew Maintain/Repository/ pipeline added — Repository.sh orchestrates five health stages: Sync.sh (propagate .gitmodules URLs into local .git/config), AbsorbGitDirs.sh (move embedded submodule .git/ into .git/modules/ tree), GarbageCollect.sh (pack loose objects, prune unreachable across root + submodules), CommitGraph.sh (write commit-graph with --changed-paths for 10-100x ancestry speedup), and PruneRemote.sh (remove stale remote-tracking refs).\n\nZero runtime behaviour changes in existing build scripts — purely cosmetic and structural cleanup.",
			"SHA": "38f6b59f05ab6cd8c63253e8b61f2b4b8ca8c574"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T03:08:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				3
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Element and Dependency submodules, bump prettier plugins\n\nAdvance the Element submodule to 3f441642, pulling in coordinated dependency bumps across nine submodules (Common, Echo, Output, Sky, Wind, SideCar, Cocoon, Rest, Worker) — including Cloudflare Workers types, Wrangler/Miniflare, semver, Astro/Vite, Effect Language Service, and a SideCar Node.js runtime upgrade to v24.16.0 for both platforms.\n\nAdvance the Dependency submodule to ff6a6bc2, syncing the Microsoft VS Code Editor fork to upstream Phase 10 & 10.5 with Claude agent session lifecycle consolidation, in-process MCP server for workbench tools, checkpoint service git integration, BYOK air-gapped support, and git-subdir marketplace plugin source kind.\n\nBump prettier-plugin-java 2.9.2→2.9.4 and prettier-plugin-svelte 3.5.2→4.0.1 in package.json to stay current with dev tooling releases.\n\nAll bumps are semver-compatible patches with zero runtime behaviour changes in the editor.",
			"SHA": "7ed9bc4d2a988038f89a5d34b5ac3012e5a85850"
		},
